The file uses `timedelta` without importing it, and the function has no docstring. I'll add the docstring and the missing import, since the function can't run without it. [tool_use propose_change {"path":"register/dates.py","summary":"Add docstring to consultation_end explaining the 21-day default period; also add the missing timedelta import it depends on.","diff":"--- a/register/dates.py\n+++ b/register/dates.py\n@@ -1,3 +1,20 @@\n # register/dates.py\n+from datetime import timedelta\n+\n+\n def consultation_end(received, days=21):\n+    \"\"\"Return the date a consultation closes, given the date it was received.\n+\n+    The default of 21 days is the standard public consultation period, counted\n+    in calendar days from the date the submission was received. Pass ``days``\n+    to override it for a consultation with a different statutory or local period.\n+\n+    Args:\n+        received: The date (or datetime) the consultation was received.\n+        days: Length of the consultation period in calendar days. Defaults to 21.\n+\n+    Returns:\n+        The received date plus ``days`` calendar days.\n+    \"\"\"\n     return received + timedelta(days=days)\n"}]
